1 0 0 1 50 582 Tm
(Abstract) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 566 Tm
(The Freedom of Information Act establishes a statutory right of access to federal) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 550 Tm
(agency records. In operational practice that right is rationed by two primary mechanisms) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 534 Tm
(that together convert the statute into a system of controlled disclosure: \(1\) strict) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 518 Tm
(processing clocks and volume limits that force agencies toward denial or minimal) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 502 Tm
(production, and \(2\) search and review fees that externalize cost onto the requester) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 486 Tm
(until the request becomes financially prohibitive. Both pathways ? information remains) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 470 Tm
(under institutional control. This paper records the binary as an observed structural) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 454 Tm
(fact rather than an administrative accident or isolated failure of implementation.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 438 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 50 422 Tm
(Keywords: Freedom of Information Act, FOIA, information access, fee barriers,) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 406 Tm
(processing delays, transparency architecture, controlled disclosure, public records.) Tj
ET
