(1. The Binary Stated) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 704 Tm
(FOIA practice, as experienced by independent requesters, reduces to a forced choice:) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 688 Tm
(Mode 1 ? Process the request under severe time and volume constraints: the agency) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 672 Tm
(denies or releases the absolute minimum that can be justified under exemption language.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 656 Tm
(Mode 2 ? Allow the request to expand in scope or volume: the agency shifts the) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 640 Tm
(financial burden onto the requester through search, review, and duplication fees until) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 624 Tm
(the cost becomes prohibitive.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 608 Tm
(Either outcome leaves the information under institutional control. Neither outcome) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 592 Tm
(constitutes freedom of information. The binary is not a rhetorical device. It is the) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 576 Tm
(practical operating surface of the statute as implemented.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 560 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 50 544 Tm
(2. Statutory Baseline) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 528 Tm
(The Freedom of Information Act, 5 U.S.C. § 552, requires federal agencies to respond to) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 512 Tm
(requests within twenty working days. ?Unusual circumstances? may extend that period by) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 496 Tm
(ten working days; further delay requires the requester?s agreement. The statute) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 480 Tm
(authorizes fees for search, review, and duplication, with different cost structures) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 464 Tm
(depending on requester category \(commercial, educational, news media, or other\).) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 448 Tm
(Public-interest fee waivers exist in the text and are discretionary in application.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 432 Tm
(These provisions create the formal architecture. The binary arises from the) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 416 Tm
(intersection of those provisions with institutional capacity, incentive structures, and) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 400 Tm
(the absence of an automatic default-to-disclosure mechanism.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 384 Tm
(Statute reference: https://www.foia.gov/) Tj
ET
endstreamendobj
