(3. Mode 1 ? Temporal and Volume Pressure) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 704 Tm
(Agencies operate under hard clocks. When a request exceeds internal processing capacity) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 688 Tm
(? illustrated by the practical threshold many requesters encounter of roughly one) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 672 Tm
(hundred pages within limited processing windows ? the rational institutional response is) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 656 Tm
(to narrow the request, invoke exemptions aggressively, issue partial releases, or deny.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 640 Tm
(The statutory clock becomes a control surface. Volume is converted into a defense. The) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 624 Tm
(agency that cannot process the full request within the allotted time is not required to) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 608 Tm
(expand its capacity; it is permitted to contract the disclosure.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 592 Tm
(This mode does not require bad faith. It requires only ordinary bureaucratic) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 576 Tm
(self-preservation under resource constraint. The statute supplies the pressure; the) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 560 Tm
(institution supplies the predictable response.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 544 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 50 528 Tm
(4. Mode 2 ? Cost as Filter) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 512 Tm
(Where the clock cannot finish the work, fees finish the selection. Search and review) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 496 Tm
(charges move the cost of institutional opacity onto the requester. A request that would) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 480 Tm
(be answerable as a matter of record becomes unanswerable as a matter of price. The) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 464 Tm
(public-interest waiver exists on the page and is not the default in the room.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 448 Tm
(Mode 2 is the second door of the same building. It does not open the file. It prices) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 432 Tm
(the file until the requester leaves.) Tj
ET
